sequenceDiagram
    actor Caller
    participant Phone as Browser Phone (POC)
    participant API as CallController
    participant Engine as ConversationEngine
    participant Khaya as Khaya ASR v3
    participant DB as Database
    Caller->>Phone: 1. Enter caller number, press Call (mic open, hands-free)
    Phone->>API: 2. POST /calls (caller_number)
    API->>Engine: 3. startCall(number, webrtc)
    Engine->>DB: 4. find Customer by phone number
    Engine-->>Phone: 5. known with saved language and remember-language on - greeting and purpose of call (skip to 14)
    Engine-->>Phone: 6. otherwise - language offers back to back - Twi (aane/1), Ewe (ɛ̃/2), English (yes/3)
    Phone-->>Caller: 7. play offers, keep listening
    Caller->>Phone: 8. speaks or presses a key while offers play
    Phone->>Phone: 9. stop prompt audio (barge-in)
    Phone->>API: 10. POST utterance WAV or keypad digit
    API->>Engine: 11. handleSpeech or handleInput
    Engine->>Khaya: 12. transcribe once in default language (twi)
    Engine->>Engine: 13. match yes-words and names of every enabled language
    Engine-->>Phone: 14. reply in chosen language - sign-up offer (unknown) or purpose of call (known)
    Phone->>API: 15. silence for 6 seconds - POST event no_input
    Engine-->>Phone: 16. replay offers (max 2 more times), then thank caller and end
    Engine-->>Phone: 17. answer not understood - say so and replay offers; 3rd in a row - explain and end call
